---
/** Monitoring and incidents as one block: what breaks, and what the team sees when it does. */
import Block from './Block.astro';
import incident from './incident.webp';
import { pack } from './packs';

/** On phones the incident screen is unreadable, so the monitors pack's phone crop stands in. */
const phone = pack('monitors').picture.phone;
---

<Block
  id="incidents"
  marker="Monitoring and incidents"
  problem="Without a DevOps engineer, monitoring is the job nobody gets to."
  title="Monitoring comes with the stack. No extra vendor."
>
  <p>
    With the Console, error tracking is on by default. Related errors, alarms and failed checks become one incident, with
    the release that was live when it opened.
  </p>
  <p class="c-small">
    Tracing is one config property and an uptime check is a URL in the config. Connect Slack to acknowledge, mute or
    roll back from the incident card.
  </p>

  <figure slot="picture" class="incidents__picture">
    <picture>
      <source
        media="(max-width: 40rem)"
        type="image/webp"
        srcset={`${phone.small.src} 1x, ${phone.large.src} 2x`}
        width={phone.small.width}
        height={phone.small.height}
      />
      <img
        class="c-frame"
        src={incident.src}
        width={incident.width}
        height={incident.height}
        loading="lazy"
        alt="An incident in the Stacktape Console: API error rate above 5% on checkout-api production, with an AI assessment and a draft fix pull request. On phones: the Requests and Errors metric cards."
      />
    </picture>
    <figcaption class="c-muted">
      <span class="incidents__wide"
        >Every incident gets an AI assessment on your organization's Anthropic, OpenAI or xAI key. Investigations and fixes
        run when you ask, on that key or your own subscription. Nothing is deployed.</span
      >
      <span class="incidents__narrow">Requests and errors for the last 24 hours, in the Console.</span>
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
</Block>

<style>
  .incidents__narrow {
    display: none;
  }

  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    .incidents__wide {
      display: none;
    }

    .incidents__narrow {
      display: inline;
    }
  }

  .incidents__picture {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--brand-space-3);
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--brand-type-sm);
  }
</style>
